<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_OcularJelly_TwitchWiring.xml: switches the zhool onto its twitching-tentacle render tree.
  STAGED (Staged/TentacleTwitch/, never loaded; held in src/DEPLOY_HOLD.txt) until the owner accepts the split art (tentacle-less bell + four tentacle pictures, all
  facings; artpipe rows tt_zhool_*_v1, design/RimMandrake/tentacle_twitch_art_rows_2026-10-15.json) and it is installed
  through art.py at the texPaths below. Go live only then: with the art missing this draws pink squares.
  The tree also needs RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.dll with PawnRenderSubWorker_KindLifeStageScale deployed.
  Design: design/RimMandrake/tentacle_twitch_design_2026-10-15.md. Tree: Staged/TentacleTwitch/Defs/PawnRenderTreeDefs/RM_OcularJelly_Twitch.xml.

  Until then the race keeps vanilla's Animal tree and its one whole-body picture (Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RM_ContagionBulloos.xml).
  Go-live: fold both operations into that def, delete this file, and move the tree into Defs/PawnRenderTreeDefs/.
  The texPath replace hits all three life stages; each keeps its own drawSize.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RM_OcularJelly"]/race</xpath>
    <value>
      <renderTree>RM_OcularJelly_Twitch</renderTree>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="RM_OcularJelly"]/lifeStages/li/bodyGraphicData/texPath</xpath>
    <value>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_OcularJelly/RM_OcularJelly_Bell</texPath>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
